<title>BELGIUM: EU says has serious doubts about Stena/P&amp;O link.</title>
<headline>EU says has serious doubts about Stena/P&amp;O link.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-06-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>The European Commission said on Wednesday it had sent P&amp;O and Stena Line a letter expressing &quot;serious doubts&quot; about their proposed ferry joint venture on the English Channel.  </p>
<p>&quot;The Commission has informed P&amp;O and Stena that it has serious doubts as to whether their proposal to combine their cross-Channel ferry services can be cleared under EC competition rules,&quot; the Commission said in a statement.</p>
<p>However, the letter did &quot;not rule out the possibility that the venture will ultimately receive clearance,&quot; the Commission added.</p>
<p>The Commission said it had received comments from a wide range of interested parties on the planned deal.</p>
<p>It gave no further details.</p>
<p>-- Brussels newsroom +32 2 287 68 11</p>
</text>
